      en: "The Addis Ababa Stadium, officially part of the city's central sports complex, is the premier sporting venue in the Ethiopian capital. Originally built in the 1940s and extensively renovated in 1999 to meet international standards, the stadium has a capacity of approximately 35,000 spectators. It serves as the home ground for the Ethiopian national football team, popularly known as the 'Walias,' and hosts major athletics competitions. Located in the heart of Addis Ababa, near the central railway station and Meskel Square, it is a key urban landmark accessible to residents and visitors alike. The stadium has been the site of numerous historic matches and continental championships, including the Africa Cup of Nations. Beyond sports, the facility is used for national celebrations, political rallies, and cultural festivals. Despite the emergence of newer stadiums, it remains a powerful symbol of Ethiopia’s athletic heritage and national pride.",
